## 1. Executive Summary

The audit delivers one reassuring finding and one urgent finding.

**The reassuring part:** LoadSaathi is *not* deindexed or penalized. Your brand keyword "loadsaathi" returns your homepage at position #1 and your login page at #2, and your social profiles (X, Facebook, Instagram, LinkedIn, GitHub) are all indexed alongside it. Your sitemap publishes 112 URLs, robots.txt is clean, your homepage has proper title, meta description, canonical tag, and Organization schema. The foundation is healthy.

**The urgent part:** For every single non-brand keyword tested — including your own core service keywords — LoadSaathi.in does **not appear anywhere in the top 10 results**. You have 30+ published blog posts and 36 dedicated route pages that are directly relevant to these searches, yet they are invisible. The audit identified the most likely technical cause: **your site is a client-side rendered single-page application (SPA)**. Every inner URL — including `/blog/rourkela-to-ranchi-trucking-rates` and `/routes/rourkela-to-ranchi` — returns an identical 22.5 KB shell HTML containing only the homepage title and no unique meta description or structured data. The page content only materializes after JavaScript runs. Google *can* render JavaScript, but the rendering is delayed, resource-intensive, and unreliable, so in practice Google is judging your inner pages as near-empty duplicates of your homepage. This almost certainly explains the zero visibility despite content you have already written.

