## 6. Priority Fix Plan

The fixes are ordered by impact-to-effort. Estimated timelines assume a typical small dev team.

### Priority 1 — Fix the rendering (1–2 weeks, blocking everything else)

Move at least your public content layer — blog posts, route pages, location pages, guides — to **server-side rendering or static site generation** so that each URL returns unique HTML with its own title, meta description, and structured data. If migrating the whole app is too heavy right now, a lighter path is **dynamic prerendering**: middleware (e.g., `@prerender/prerender-middleware` or a Cloudflare Workers script) that serves a fully rendered HTML snapshot to bots while regular users still get the SPA. This alone is very likely to move dozens of your existing pages from invisible to ranked within 4–12 weeks of re-crawl.

### Priority 2 — Add unique per-page metadata (during the same sprint)

Every route page needs a title in Trukky's style: *"Rourkela to Ranchi Truck Rate 2026 — ₹X/km, Book PTL & FTL Online | LoadSaathi"*. Every blog post needs a unique title + 150–160 character description. Add `Article` JSON-LD to blog posts, `Product/Offer` or `Service` schema with price ranges to route pages, and `FAQPage` schema where questions exist. Submit the updated sitemap to Google Search Console and request re-indexing of the top 20 URLs via URL Inspection.

### Priority 3 — Verify what Google actually sees (this week, free)

Open **Google Search Console → URL Inspection** and test `/blog/rourkela-to-ranchi-trucking-rates` and `/routes/rourkela-to-ranchi`. Check the "View Crawled Page" screenshot: if it shows an empty or shell-only page, the rendering diagnosis is confirmed. Also check the **Page Indexing** report for "Crawled — currently not indexed" counts, and the **Top pages** report to see which URLs Google has indexed at all. If you can share a GSC screenshot, I can refine this report further. (Bing Webmaster Tools is a free alternative that confirms the same signals.)

### Priority 4 — Target winnable long-tail variants first

While the render fix propagates, shift target keywords to variants your East India moat actually matches, where the SERP is weaker:

| Instead of | Target | Why it is winnable |
|---|---|---|
| PTL transport India | PTL transport in Odisha / Jharkhand / West Bengal | National 3PLs ignore state-level long-tail; you own these markets |
| return load app India | return loads Rourkela / return load trucks Ranchi to Kolkata | Regional, exact-fit with your existing guide content |
| e-way bill rules 2026 | e-way bill rules for transporters and truckers 2026 | Excludes the ClearTax/CBIC authority sites; serves your actual audience |
| transport service in Rourkela | transport service in Rourkela for steel / goods carrier Rourkela to Ranchi | Dodges the directory pack; matches your industrial audience |

### Priority 5 — Build authority on the region (ongoing)

Register and optimize a **Google Business Profile** for LoadSaathi (local pack entries — VRL, TCI Express, SafeExpress currently own the map results for "transport service in Rourkela"), collect trucker and shipper reviews, and pursue regional backlinks (Odisha/Jharkhand business directories, local news mentions, trade associations). Each route page should also internally link to your fare calculator and the related blog post, forming a topic cluster.

